        <constraint id="9198-0cde-c6b2-9ef2" type="max" value="1" scope="parent" field="selections" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
        <constraint id="6898-9444-c337-e89c" type="max" value="1" scope="roster" field="selections" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule id="9909-28ed-a135-f4a0" name="Special character" hidden="false">
          <description>Unique named selection. 205 points includes the complete listed fixed equipment, companions, powers and mounts; only separately offered options add points. Printed profiles are before magic-item bonuses unless a rule says they are already included. Special-character use requires the players’ agreement under the books’ convention.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="bbcd-57e6-9b25-b7bc" name="Included equipment" hidden="false">
          <description>Sword; lance; heavy armour; shield.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="619c-d47f-f0f7-aa14" name="Jules" hidden="false" publicationId="ef30-8d5f-80e5-af93" page="72">
          <description>Unarmoured, with a hand weapon, on foot but keeps pace with Tristan. Weapons and missiles hit him only on a 6. Tristan’s opponent tests Leadership against Jules’s taunts; failure costs its first attack. If Jules dies or leaves the battlefield, Tristan cannot sing for the rest of the battle. Reference: Bretonnia, printed p. 72.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="80c1-571c-a10d-0ea0" name="Songs of Noble Valour" hidden="false" publicationId="ef30-8d5f-80e5-af93" page="72">
          <description>At the start of a Bretonnian turn, choose one song if Tristan accompanies a regiment; it lasts until the start of the next Bretonnian turn and may be renewed or changed. Bataille: unit +1 combat result. Grail: natural dispel 3+ against spells affecting Tristan or his unit. Gilles: unit Leadership 10. Songs cease if Tristan is slain or cannot sing. Reference: Bretonnia, printed p. 72.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink id="f6fd-c5fd-8eb1-25ca" name="Questing Virtue" targetId="325a-85cf-1566-61ec" type="rule" hidden="false" publicationId="ef30-8d5f-80e5-af93" page="48" />
        <infoLink id="bcb7-be9d-b895-b49d" name="Virtue of Noble Disdain" targetId="a4ee-13ca-e4fe-6d22" type="rule" hidden="false" publicationId="ef30-8d5f-80e5-af93" page="49" />
        <infoLink id="78a5-cdae-f7f2-0c7d" name="Lance" targetId="95b2-3266-1f10-e5fa" type="rule" hidden="false" publicationId="d7c9-7773-4408-58f6" page="55" />
